    <section id="faqs" class="section section-alt">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header">
          <span class="section-tag"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-question"></i> Help Center</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <p class="section-subtitle">Find immediate answers to common questions about cloud storage architecture and security.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Live FAQ Search Filter -->
        <div class="faq-search-box">
          <i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass"></i>
          <input type="text" id="faq-search-input" placeholder="Search FAQs (e.g. Encryption, Backup, Limits)...">
        </div>

        <div class="faq-accordion">
          <!-- FAQ 1 -->
          <div class="glass-card faq-item open">
            <div class="faq-question">
              <span>What encryption standard is used to secure files?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-toggle-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              All stored files are encrypted using Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) with 256-bit symmetric keys before being written to disk. Key rotation is managed via Cloud Key Management Services (KMS).
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ 2 -->
          <div class="glass-card faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">
              <span>How does the system ensure data redundancy and high availability?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-toggle-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              Files are automatically replicated across a minimum of 3 availability zones within the primary cloud region, guaranteeing 99.999999999% (11 9s) data durability.
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ 3 -->
          <div class="glass-card faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">
              <span>What is the maximum file size limit for uploads?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-toggle-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              Through S3 multipart chunked uploads, single file payloads up to 5 Terabytes (TB) are supported smoothly through the web browser and API clients.
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ 4 -->
          <div class="glass-card faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">
              <span>Can deleted files be recovered?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-toggle-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              Yes, deleted files are retained in the system Trash bin for 30 days. Furthermore, bucket versioning maintains older point-in-time file states for instant rollbacks.
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ 5 -->
          <div class="glass-card faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">
              <span>How are file share links protected against unauthorized access?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-toggle-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              Share links can be configured with custom expiration timestamps, mandatory access passcodes, max-download counters, and IP whitelist restrictions.
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ 6 -->
          <div class="glass-card faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">
              <span>What happens if internet connectivity drops during an upload?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-toggle-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              Our upload manager uses resumable protocol chunking. Once internet connection is re-established, the upload resumes from the exact byte offset without restarting.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

